\code{pres_train <- pres_data[!result$pres_selected_idx, ]}

\code{bg_test    <- bg_data[result$bg_selected_idx, ]}

\code{bg_train   <- bg_data[!result$bg_selected_idx, ]}
}
\section{Interpretation of missing fold IDs}{


With \code{include_na = FALSE}, missing fold IDs are outside the selection
problem. They are included in \code{n_pres_total} or \code{n_bg_total}, but excluded
from \code{n_pres_in_scope} or \code{n_bg_in_scope}.

With \code{include_na = TRUE}, all missing fold IDs are treated as belonging to
one common fold named \code{"<NA>"}. Therefore, selecting that fold selects every
record with a missing fold ID in the corresponding dataset.

To avoid ambiguity when \code{include_na = TRUE}, the input fold identifiers
are not allowed to contain an actual, non-missing fold ID equal to \code{"<NA>"}.
}

